    <string-array name="walkthrough_bodies">
        <item>An independent studio. Calm software, no dark patterns, no accounts, no data sold. VividOrbit is our living-room app.</item>
        <item>A lineup manager for the tuner already in this box. It does not stream the internet and does not replace your cable or DTH service.</item>
        <item>GUIDE opens the list. Up from the first row reaches All / Favorites. Left opens categories. Right shows now and next. Settings is the top-right control.</item>
        <item>Open Settings. Turn Custom Channel Numbers ON. OK a channel in the list below to type a number. If that number is taken, the two channels swap. Auto-number 1-N or Reset to DTH sit under the toggle.</item>
        <item>In Settings, pick Last watched, First in list, or a fixed default. Long-press OK on a channel in the guide to set it as the startup channel.</item>
        <item>Settings → Button mapper lets you bind zap, guide, info, last-channel, and favorites to whatever keys your remote actually has.</item>
        <item>Settings → Phone Setup shows a QR. Scan it on the same Wi-Fi to reorder, renumber, hide, and tune. The page lives on this TV and stops when you close the panel.</item>
        <item>No accounts, ads, or analytics. If the list is empty, run a channel scan in the system Live TV settings first, then come back.</item>
    </string-array>
